    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0364" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">358.116 M 82/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-04-28T15:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 28,
                                1921—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 28—1:56
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>46. Your 21, April 9, 6 p.m. and 23, April 26, 6 p.m.<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d199-f1"/> Since my report, telegram number 43, April 9, 11 a.m., no
                    change in conditions. <pb facs="0365" n="251" xml:id="pg251"/> The two
                    missionaries who had received notice of the cancellation of their visas are
                    still here although the period of their original permission to remain in Sweden
                    has expired and they have not been asked to leave the country. Have today
                    received following note from Foreign Office in reply to request to send
                    investigator to Utah.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“In response to this communication I have the honor to call to your attention
                        that the Royal Government does not believe that it should accept this
                        invitation as the conditions to be looked into are already sufficiently
                        known from reports of persons worthy of credence who have been sent there by
                        the Government for the purpose of giving an account of the state of affairs
                        in the Mormon Church and community.”</p></quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
